## Purpose

Make the hosted Work tab a fast operational answer to what remains, where every item belongs, and
what should be done next, while preserving the flat ledger as an explicit audit view.

## Desired Outcome

The dashboard opens on a deterministic Remaining Tree projected from locally authoritative
relationships and order. Every visible governed item appears once as a root or owned child;
invalid placement is explicit, filters retain ancestry, whole roots stay intact, one honest Next
marker guides execution, and safe row menus copy allowlisted Tool Shed commands without executing
them.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Projection contract | Exact remaining membership, canonical placement, order, ancestry, and root pagination | reported work inventory |
| Operator presentation | Default expandable tree, explicit list audit mode, state columns, counts, and safe command menus | projection contract |
| Portable release | Focused, full, Linux, Windows, release, production, and immediate-convergence evidence | both implementation workstreams |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-REMAINING-PLACEMENT-CONTRACT` — exact remaining membership and one canonical placement.
2. `G2-HIERARCHY-ORDER-CONTEXT` — deterministic order, ancestry under narrowing, truthful Next,
   and root-preserving pagination.
3. `G3-DEFAULT-TREE-LIST-PARITY` — useful default tree, retained ledger, state, and accessibility.
4. `G4-BOUNDED-COMMAND-MENUS` — descriptive, allowlisted, clipboard-only artifact actions.
5. `G5-CROSS-LANE-PRODUCTION-PROOF` — Linux, Windows, release, deployment, and immediate
   production convergence.

## Program Shape

1. Build and prove the projection and interaction as a Work2 candidate.
2. Qualify every gate cross-platform, release the exact candidate, deploy production, verify the
   live IDEA-0023 chain immediately, and recursively reconcile through Work5.

## Completion Boundary

The map is complete only when all five readiness gates are satisfied by one released exact commit,
all configured production lanes converge, and Campaign, PRM, Map, and Idea outcomes are closed and
reconciled.
